# sound_eat: eating food plays the chew cue (SFX_EAT). The harness fires the
# local chew cue on the `eat` verb (the GLFW F-to-eat path that normally plays
# it does not run headless); the actual hunger restore stays server-authoritative.
# item 50 = ITEM_COOKED_BEEF. We lower hunger and give the food to the server so
# an eat is plausible, then eat and assert the cue fired. (We do NOT assert the
# food shows in the client inventory or that hunger changed: the client's
# PKT_INVENTORY handler currently filters food ids, so the eat cue — which fires
# locally on the verb — is the robust signal here.)
# Counters start at zero each run, so any nonzero count == the SFX fired.
> {"cmd":"step","ticks":20}
expect sounds.eat == 0
> {"cmd":"set_food","value":6}
> {"cmd":"give","item":50,"count":3}
> {"cmd":"step","ticks":6}
> {"cmd":"eat"}
> {"cmd":"step","ticks":6}
# The chew cue fired.
expect sounds.eat > 0
